Fix OOB free in the MOV demuxer's STSD parser (FFmpeg n6.1.1).

Upstream commit a58cb16e27bc0c32906cfb3de36e4a495c0a8602 (Ted Meyer, 2026-02-03),
not present in n6.1.1 which prepare.py pins.

mov_read_stsd() leaves sc->stsd_count stale when ff_mov_read_stsd_entries()
fails partway, while freeing and NULLing sc->extradata/extradata_size. A root
level stsd that fails, followed by a second one that succeeds, then passes the
"Duplicate stsd" guard and allocates a smaller array while the counter keeps
counting up. mov_read_close() then walks sc->stsd_count entries past the end of
that array and calls av_free() on whatever heap data follows it.

Reachable from a plain .mp4: a crafted sidx sets frag_index.complete, which
makes mov_read_default() defer trailing root atoms to mov_switch_root() during
packet reading, giving the two parse passes the desync needs.

diff --git a/libavformat/mov.c b/libavformat/mov.c
index 606fe22..f06ff0c 100644
--- a/libavformat/mov.c
+++ b/libavformat/mov.c
@@ -2871,6 +2871,7 @@ fail:
             av_freep(&sc->extradata[j]);
     }
 
+    sc->stsd_count = 0;
     av_freep(&sc->extradata);
     av_freep(&sc->extradata_size);
     return ret;
